["beyondthebump-1xbjkpj","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","pain",["feeding_to_sleep","early_waking","sleep_training_values"],"about 50% of the time she'll wake up around 4am and will not go back to sleep without nursing and she won't let me put her down. She wakes up around 8am so that's 4 hours of nursing every morning.","Eleven-month-old; mother doesn't want to sleep train but is at wits' end."],
["beyondthebump-1xbjkpj","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","tried_failed",["night_weaning","feeding_to_sleep"],"My plan was to wean her when she got her first tooth, but that was at 4 months so it didn't happen. then I said when she gets her top teeth, now I'm saying 1 year is my limit, but I honestly have no idea how we're going to do this without sleep training her.","Weaning deadlines keep moving."],
["beyondthebump-1xbjkpj","19rfii9wm6hk1","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","belief",["night_wakings","comparison_other_babies"],"People say newborn trenches but it's definitely 1 year trenches over here. I definitely thought she'd be sleeping through the night be 12 months!","Expectation that sleep would be solved by one year."],
["beyondthebump-1xbjkpj","19rfvuj0do3fp","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","tried_failed",["partner_disagreement","cry_it_out","guilt"],"I can def sleep train, and we tried it before, but my husband loses his mind so we have to stop haha it's heartbreaking and I hate it but I know she'll be okay and we'll all be sleeping better after","Husband can't tolerate the crying, so sleep training stopped."],
["beyondthebump-1xblg5d","","new_mother","baby_5_8_months","pain",["night_wakings","feeding_to_sleep","parent_body","maternal_exhaustion"],"Recently , I have been absolutely shivering when waking up. Like a tremor almost ? It usually lasts a few moments and then I just feel it internal . It’s extremely unsettling . I’m not going to the doctor because I know it’s exhaustion .","Mother of a 6.5-month-old waking every two hours to comfort nurse."],
["NewParents-1xblgzo","","new_mother","baby_2_4_months","trigger_moment",["transition_to_cot","night_wakings","parent_work_impact"],"He finally fell asleep at 6am and I have to wake up for work at 7am and really struggling.","Three-month-old moved to crib, waking 20 minutes after every transfer; mother back at work."],
["NewParents-1xblgzo","","new_mother","baby_2_4_months","pain",["maternal_exhaustion","sleep_training_values"],"I don’t want to let him cry it out but am open to other sleep training I guess? I just can’t go on like this. It has me sobbing in the middle of the night because I am so tired.","Asks for any and all 'constructive' feedback."],
["NewParents-1xblgzo","19rfmtm5f4c1s","new_mother","baby_2_4_months","pain",["partner_split_nights","parent_work_impact"],"I was on my own last night as he was on a business trip. I’m trying to tag him in when I hit my limit as he usually is able to sleep through his cries.","Partner travels for work and sleeps through crying."],
["NewParents-1xblgzo","19rfob6mn0xkx","new_mother","baby_2_4_months","pain",["daycare","relative_caregiver_conflict","parent_work_impact"],"I’m trying to get more daytime calories in him too but I’m back at work so am at the mercy of daycare and his grandmas watching him during the day.","Can't control daytime feeding while at work."],
["NewParents-1xblgzo","19rfrp65j27es","new_mother","baby_2_4_months","pain",["parent_work_impact"],"USA baby 😒","Replying to why she's back at work at three months."],
["NewParents-1xblksb","","new_mother","baby_5_8_months","pain",["only_mum_settles","bedtime_battle","contact_naps"],"since he hit 6 months I can't get away without him waking up 5 mins later and crying for me. It's been 3.5weeks of it now and im finding it very difficult. I am in bed every evening now from 6/7pm because he cries and cries unless I take him to bed at that time.","Breastfeeding mother of a high-needs 6-month-old."],
["NewParents-1xblksb","","new_mother","baby_5_8_months","pain",["marriage_strain","partner_split_nights"],"I miss my partner, we never get alone time without baby now (our families live hours away) and he sleeps in the spare bed because my son wakes on average 4/5 times a night and since I breastfeed exclusively there's no point him waking up too.","Evenings and nights lost to the baby."],
["NewParents-1xblksb","","new_mother","baby_5_8_months","belief",["sleep_training_values","gentle_method"],"I'm not going to 'sleep train' my son, I don't believe in it, I'm prepared to give him what he clearly needs and hope that this is temporary until he's a little older.","Pre-empts sleep training replies; asks only for solidarity."],
["NewParents-1xblksb","","new_mother","baby_5_8_months","question",["only_mum_settles"],"How long did it last? Did anything help? Is it this normal? Any ideas for me to do anything other than watch netflix behind his head each night?!","Asks for others who went through it."],
["sleeptrain-1xbllzy","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","success_story",["gentle_method","temperament"],"We never did any formal sleep training (no Ferber, CIO, etc.) as it just didn't work for us due to our living situation and baby’s temperament but over time we did a gentler fading method and landed on a routine that works pretty well for us on **most** nights","Fading with humming for an 11-month-old."],
["sleeptrain-1xbllzy","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","fear",["gentle_method"],"As he grows older and becomes more aware of me leaving the room (and once he learns to sit up/stand in the crib), will this routine likely fall apart?","Worried a working gentle routine won't survive toddlerhood."],
["sleeptrain-1xbmvf3","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","tried_failed",["night_wakings","white_noise","transition_to_cot"],"I feel like I’ve tried everything, different types of sleep sacks, sound machines, crib in my room, in his own room, different bed times, laying him down drowsy, laying him down once he’s asleep and he still wakes up every 2-3 hours ATLEAST.","Eight-month-old with CMPA at daycare."],
["sleeptrain-1xbmvf3","19rfpkvdxv70g","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","pain",["daycare_naps","schedule_rigidity"],"No that is mandated nap time. I tried to cap the first one but then he was too tired and just screamed all morning….","Daycare sets the nap times she's told to change."],
["sleeptrain-1xbpbuq","","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["chair_method","maternal_exhaustion"],"in reality naps are now becoming a struggle too, with her wanting us to stay. We are burnt out.","Repost to r/sleeptrain of the three-year-old regression after holiday."],
["sleeptrain-1xbpbuq","19rfuhvifs1j4","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","question",["schedule_rigidity","information_overload"],"I’m not following and not quite sure what I’m doing wrong","Replying to a commenter's sleep-hour arithmetic."],
["sleeptrain-1xbpbuq","19rg285ocnpoh","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","belief",["schedule_rigidity","drop_nap","free_advice_wins"],"a mistake I have been making is that I’ve been calculating from when physically asleep, I should be counting from when she goes to bed (and making that later). So I think I’m offering more sleep than she realistically will have because her sleep needs have recently transition from 12-ish to 11-ish hours","Two commenters' exact sleep math changes her plan."],
["sleeptrain-1xbpbuq","19rgx8a6huu9u","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","success_story",["free_advice_wins","schedule_rigidity"],"She slept through! I’m sure it’s not going to be perfect but a reprieve for us. Lights out at 9pm (she was actually asleep at 9:30pm)","First night after moving bedtime later on commenters' numbers."],
["NewParents-1xbpzm7","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","pain",["night_wakings","maternal_exhaustion"],"Its 1am as I type this - I haven't had the chance to go to bed at all tonight. Even if she falls asleep right now, she will probably wake up in a couple hours and we'll have to do it all over again. I feel so defeated.","New skill keeps waking the baby in the cot; feeding to sleep stopped working."],
["toddlers-1xbqbwk","","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","question",["night_wakings","room_sharing"],"The issue is they share the room so if the little one is crying loudly the older may wake up too. It may take a few weeks of exhaustion for both kids, I understand.","Siblings aged 2 and 5 share a room and come out at night."],
["toddlers-1xbqbwk","","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["daycare_naps","bedtime_battle"],"Part of the issue of this is the little one naps at her daycare/school, which makes her not tired enough to sleep, so she keeps coming out of the room and crying.","Daycare nap pushes bedtime late."],
["sleeptrain-1xbry2d","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","pain",["ferber","night_wakings"],"Because crying is so on and off I feel unsure how to do intervals. I try to wait for continuous crying but he never reaches five minutes continuously. So I don’t go in and comfort for up to an hour most of the time.","Logs a minute-by-minute 3am wake on Ferber night 5."],
["sleeptrain-1xbry2d","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","desire",["ferber","travel_disruption","maternal_exhaustion"],"I’m desperate to have him trained soon since I haven’t slept in five months and we are traveling soon, and I think training will be harder once we do.","Racing to finish Ferber before a trip."],
["sleeptrain-1xbry2d","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","question",["ferber","wake_windows","schedule_rigidity"],"Can Ferber or sleep training work so long as the baby has lots of wake time, even if we aren’t consistent with precise nap times?","Lifestyle means babywearing and variable naps."],
["sleeptrain-1xbry2d","19rg665hymxls","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","belief",["ferber","night_weaning","books"],"The Ferber book in fact states that 5 months old do not require any night feeds, although they can be continued. I’d much prefer for the little man to eat more in the day time.","Following the book while cutting night feeds."],
["sleeptrain-1xbryo5","","parent_unspecified","baby_9_12_months","tried_failed",["retraining_after_setback","cry_it_out"],"baby has been teething real bad the past few weeks and it’s completely derailed her sleep. She was sleep trained around 6 months using cio but now we are retraining once again. Last night was night 3 and it took her about 3 mins of crying thankfully.","Retraining a 13-month-old after teething."],
["sleeptrain-1xbryo5","","parent_unspecified","baby_9_12_months","fear",["low_sleep_needs","short_naps"],"I did recently reduce her nap by 15 minutes bc when she has motn wakes it usually means she’s getting too much nap time but I feel like she barely sleeps as it is so I’m nervous I’m making her overtired now. She at baseline is a low sleep needs baby.","Rules of thumb pull against her baby's low sleep needs."],
["NewParents-1xbvmk1","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","belief",["cry_it_out","guilt","sleep_training_values"],"I’m not one for the cry it out method because I feel like I’m letting her down and breaking her trust that mama’s always gonna be there when she calls.","Day one of moving a 9.5-month-old to her own space."],
